  "question": {
    "text": "Monochromatic light of wavelength $500 \\mathrm{~nm}$ is used in Young's double slit experiment. An interference pattern is obtained on a screen. When one of the slits is covered with a very thin glass plate (refractive index $=1.5$ ), the central maximum is shifted to a position previously occupied by the $4^{\\text {th }}$ bright fringe. The thickness of the glass-plate is ______ $\\mu \\mathrm{m}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & (\\mu-1) \\mathrm{t}=\\mathrm{n} \\lambda \\\\ & (1.5-1) \\mathrm{t}=4 \\times 500 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{~m} \\\\ & \\mathrm{t}=4000 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{~m} \\\\ & \\mathrm{t}=4 \\mu \\mathrm{m}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
